.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH scanr-transport-test 1  "scanr-transport-test " 
.SH NAME
scanr\-transport\-test \- Measure a proxy\*(Aqs reachability, authentication, and result fidelity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\-transport\-test\fR [\fB\-\-known\-open\fR] [\fB\-\-known\-closed\fR] [\fB\-\-calibrate\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Measure a proxy\*(Aqs reachability, authentication, and result fidelity
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-known\-open\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Destination expected to be open; defaults to the proxy\*(Aqs own address
.TP
\fB\-\-known\-closed\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Destination expected to be closed; defaults to port 1 on the proxy host
.TP
\fB\-\-calibrate\fR
Also sweep concurrency to find where this proxy starts refusing connections. Generates real traffic and takes about a minute
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

